@startuml boomletwo_checkpoint_recovery
title Self-contained DIGGING checkpoint and guarded Boomletwo recovery
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
participant "Original Boomlet" as B
participant Niso as N
participant WT as W
participant "Other peers" as P
participant "Designated offline Boomletwo" as T
actor "User with enrolled ST" as U

note over B,T
  Setup has authorized exactly this backup target.
  Neither ST nor Boomletwo records each ordinary transition.
  The checkpoint format below is a candidate extension.
end note

group Normal DIGGING
  B -> B: Validate ordinary progress and preserve exact SAR duty
  B -> B: Create target-encrypted checkpoint and exact placeholder
  B -> B: Bind checkpoint digest in existing signed ping
  B -> N: Signed ping bundle with detached encrypted checkpoint
  N -> W: Ordinary authenticated submission with recovery bundle
  W -> P: Retain checkpoint evidence under the candidate distribution policy
  W -> W: Collect five pings and exact recipient SAR acknowledgments
  W -> B: Candidate shared five-ping pong and own SAR acknowledgment
  B -> B: Match own returned ping; verify the other four\nKeep ordinary counter and SAR guards
end

... Original Boomlet is lost; no further source interaction ...

group Inspect a recovery checkpoint
  U -> T: Start recovery using designated setup backup
  N -> T: Retained ping bundle and required public evidence
  P -> T: Existing WT activation record and available decision evidence
  T -> T: Verify source signature and exact encrypted checkpoint\nBind setup, target, withdrawal, sequence and placeholder
  T -> T: Identify WT at the checkpoint using retained head\nDo not treat peer claims as latest-state authority
  note over N,T
    A valid old ping can omit a later duress duty or WT vote.
    Source loss claims do not prove that an isolated source cannot return.
  end note
end

alt Complete activation safeguards have been established
  T -> T: Bind checkpoint and attempt irreversibly\nGenerate and persist one independent draw R
  T -> T: For unreached state use max(original mystery, R)\nor setup upper bound plus R
  T -> T: Restore only authenticated progress and exact duties\nContinue ordinary gates under a defined exclusion mechanism
else Exclusion or later security state is unresolved
  T -> T: Do not enable signing, WT voting or new counter progress
end

note over B,T
  No source retirement message or continuous ST service is assumed.
  Historical pongs and ping counts cannot earn new counter increments.
  This checkpoint mechanism alone is not a complete activation protocol.
end note
@enduml
